<https://zbmath.org/review/592617> a schema:Review ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:itemReviewed zbmath:592617 ;
    schema:reviewAspect "review" ;
    schema:reviewBody """A statistical-mechanical treatment of equilibrium flows in the two- dimensional Euler fluid is constructed which respects all conservation laws. The techniques may be generalized to a number of Coulomb-like Hamiltonian systems with an infinite number of conservation laws, including some in higher dimensions. Our results may be applicable to cylindrically bounded guiding-center plasmas, which under idealized conditions provide another realization of two-dimensional Euler flow. Finally, a phenomenological theory of the weakly driven, weakly damped Euler fluid, based on weak perturbations of the equilibrium state, is presented. A very simple two-parameter model is used to illustrate the principal ideas.

For the entire collection see [Zbl 0787.00033].""" .

<https://zbmath.org/review/592618> a schema:Review ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:itemReviewed zbmath:592618 ;
    schema:reviewAspect "review" ;
    schema:reviewBody """This paper surveys the theory and applications of solutions of the Burgers' equation with random initial data which are often called statistical solution. It is far from complete and reflects only the author's own interests. A description of other recent developments can be found in the bibliography.

For the entire collection see [Zbl 0787.00033].""" .

