<https://zbmath.org/review/592629> a schema:Review ;
    dcterms:creator <https://zbmath.org/authors/schirotzek.winfried> ;
    schema:inLanguage "English" ;
    schema:itemReviewed zbmath:592629 ;
    schema:reviewAspect "review" ;
    schema:reviewBody """Let \\(A\\) be a subset of a Riemannian manifold such that any two points of \\(A\\) are joined by a geodesic belonging to \\(A\\). A function \\(f: A\\to \\mathbb{R}\\) is said to be geodesic convex if the restriction of \\(f\\) to each geodesic arc belonging to \\(A\\) is convex in the arc length parameter. The author discusses this and related concepts such as (local) geodesic quasiconvexity.

For the entire collection see [Zbl 0788.00061].""" ;
    schema:reviewer <https://zbmath.org/authors/schirotzek.winfried> .

